1
00:00:09,270 --> 00:00:10,350
(Passenger Drop-off Area)

2
00:00:36,330 --> 00:00:39,350
=Vow of Autumn=
=Episode 16=

3
00:00:57,580 --> 00:00:58,200
(Have a try.)

4
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:02,760
(Louder!)

5
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:17,560
(Feel better now?)

6
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:21,960
(When I'm upset,)

7
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:23,280
(I like coming here.)

8
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:25,080
(The first time)

9
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:27,920
(was the year my parents divorced.)

10
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:31,080
(Back then,)

11
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:32,760
(I felt so lonely.)

12
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:36,320
(As if I'd suddenly lost my dad.)

13
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:39,980
(My mom tried so hard to love me.)

14
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:41,400
(She gave me everything.)

15
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:44,640
(But growing up, I still often)

16
00:01:46,180 --> 00:01:47,760
(felt unloved.)

17
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:51,400
(Now I understand.)

18
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:54,440
(Being an adult is not easy.)

19
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:57,020
(Sometimes, it's not that
they don't love you.)

20
00:01:58,460 --> 00:02:00,100
(They just don't have the time.)

21
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:06,120
(Qiu,)

22
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:08,560
(you're allowed to resent your mom.)

23
00:02:08,640 --> 00:02:09,640
(You have that right.)

24
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:13,040
(But there must be a misunderstanding.)

25
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:16,280
(Being a good stepmom is hard.)

26
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:19,600
(She's trying to be there
for all three of you.)

27
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:21,360
(It's not easy for her.)

28
00:02:21,980 --> 00:02:23,780
(It's not that
she doesn't want to.)

29
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:26,260
(She just doesn't know how.)

30
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:38,540
And

31
00:02:40,420 --> 00:02:41,260
then what happened?

32
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:44,620
I don't know what she said to Mom.

33
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:48,060
I just remember, that night,

34
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:50,740
Mom knocked on my door

35
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:52,920
and talked to me for a long time.

36
00:02:54,380 --> 00:02:55,300
She cried.

37
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:57,180
So did I.

38
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:01,060
For me,

39
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:03,060
it was only after that day

40
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:05,180
that our family

41
00:03:05,460 --> 00:03:07,060
really felt like a family.

42
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:19,960
I'll never forget

43
00:03:21,580 --> 00:03:22,880
the first person

44
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:25,280
who made me feel truly seen.

45
00:03:26,260 --> 00:03:26,920
It was her.

46
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:44,660
I'm sorry.

47
00:03:48,220 --> 00:03:49,380
I had no idea.

48
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:13,000
You'd better treat her well.

49
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:14,400
I'm warning you.

50
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:15,620
Between you and her,

51
00:04:15,620 --> 00:04:16,480
I'm on her side.

52
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:17,640
If you ever hurt her...

53
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:18,380
I won't.

54
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:23,660
I'll never hurt her.

55
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:47,240
You're back.

56
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:50,640
What's wrong?

57
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:55,160
What did you say to her?

58
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:56,040
Why was she crying?

59
00:04:57,940 --> 00:04:59,200
Nothing.

60
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:02,100
It was something else.

61
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:09,060
Okay.

62
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:10,980
What about breakfast?

63
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:11,780
I'll order in.

64
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:14,120
Why order in?

65
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:18,020
Don't you know he's a great cook?

66
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:21,040
He did study abroad
for a few years, after all.

67
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:23,280
Just wait.

68
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:24,360
Let's sit and wait.

69
00:05:37,340 --> 00:05:38,180
Well?

70
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:39,900
My brother

71
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:41,060
is quite a catch, huh?

72
00:05:46,960 --> 00:05:48,100
When will Gu Yuan come over

73
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:49,080
so we can meet properly?

74
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:53,640
We'll see.

75
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:56,480
We've made up,

76
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:58,760
but we're not official yet.

77
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:00,120
Then make the first move.

78
00:06:00,640 --> 00:06:01,700
Not unless he does.

79
00:06:01,780 --> 00:06:03,220
I'm not going first.

80
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:06,100
Don't you call yourself
a modern, independent woman?

81
00:06:06,100 --> 00:06:07,320
So why not just do it?

82
00:06:07,620 --> 00:06:08,620
No.

83
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:10,700
It has to be him.

84
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:13,320
All right.

85
00:06:13,820 --> 00:06:15,060
Whatever you say.

86
00:06:15,760 --> 00:06:16,600
Anyway,

87
00:06:17,140 --> 00:06:18,460
I'm with you either way.

88
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:22,760
You're so sweet.

89
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:25,100
A great best friend

90
00:06:25,660 --> 00:06:28,120
and an even better sister-in-law.

91
00:06:29,380 --> 00:06:30,040
Su Mu!

92
00:06:30,580 --> 00:06:31,860
So you're the big sister now?

93
00:06:31,860 --> 00:06:32,920
How?

94
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:35,440
You are my sister-in-law.

95
00:06:35,440 --> 00:06:36,420
Your choice.

96
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:38,920
From now on,

97
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:41,600
you're supposed to bring me
gifts on holidays.

98
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:42,880
You wish!

99
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:44,680
We're nowhere near that yet.

100
00:06:45,140 --> 00:06:45,980
What about my gift?

101
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:47,460
Don't get ahead of yourself.

102
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:48,260
If

103
00:06:48,960 --> 00:06:50,740
things do get serious...

104
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:52,340
I won't marry him!

105
00:06:53,740 --> 00:06:55,120
You're impossible!

106
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:56,220
I'll ask my brother, then.

107
00:06:56,220 --> 00:06:57,880
When's breakfast ready?

108
00:06:58,440 --> 00:06:59,360
You two keep chatting.

109
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:00,360
I'm almost done.

110
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:13,460
Wait.

111
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:15,980
So those egg tarts I saw at your place,

112
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:17,620
was that what my brother

113
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,600
lined up to buy just for you?

114
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:25,420
Pei Yiqiu!

115
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:26,940
Choosing her over your sister?

116
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:28,120
I love egg tarts too!

117
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,400
I've asked you so many times,

118
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:30,880
and you never bought me one.

119
00:07:31,580 --> 00:07:32,300
Fine.

120
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:33,640
When I go tomorrow,

121
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:34,640
I'll get you an extra.

122
00:07:35,620 --> 00:07:36,900
So I'm just an extra?

123
00:07:41,400 --> 00:07:42,860
You're not worth wasting food on.

124
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:44,920
All right, you two. Let's eat.

125
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,040
Egg tarts tomorrow!

126
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:47,840
Fine. Two boxes tomorrow.

127
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:48,960
One extra for you.

128
00:07:52,100 --> 00:07:52,920
An extra?

129
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:54,660
You're taking her side over your family?

130
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:55,820
What, I'm not family?

131
00:07:55,900 --> 00:07:57,060
How is that taking sides?

132
00:07:58,100 --> 00:07:58,980
I'm not family?

133
00:08:00,360 --> 00:08:01,980
But he won't buy me egg tarts.

134
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:03,040
Only for you.

135
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:03,880
Then no egg tarts.

136
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:05,760
Teaming up on me now?

137
00:08:28,750 --> 00:08:30,590
(Passenger Drop-off Area)
